  message: "Closed by PR #3603 (merged). Landed all five concrete edits from the spec: .github/workflows/release.yml build loop now includes hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer; packages/hypergumbo/pyproject.toml gained a [rust-analyzer] extra pinned to ==<meta_version>; scripts/prepare-release echoes the rust-analyzer line; CHANGELOG.md got an [Unreleased] entry; packages/hypergumbo/tests/test_meta.py got two regression-guard tests (extra defined + version pin matches project.version). Scope-expanded mid-PR per user follow-up: cmd_add_extras / cmd_remove_extras now cover rust-analyzer too (the hand-coded umbrella had drifted from the WI-huham declarative table) — add-extras gates on the BUG-06 SCIP integration package the same way cmd_install_rust_analyzer does, and remove-extras uninstalls the rustup binary via uninstall_rust_analyzer. Help strings on both subparsers updated. The actual PyPI publish is gated on the next human-driven tag-release VERSION; until then, config is prepared. Out-of-scope follow-up: cmd_install_extras (WI-huham) calls install_rust_analyzer directly via _extras_components, bypassing the BUG-06 gate — same class of gap as add-extras had, separate code path."  # b3c8
